WEBVTT

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:10.000
The 7th Space War, a conflict that arose from...

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.670
...a single colony's independence movement,

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:17.640
caused catastrophic damage to Earth, the home of all mankind.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.100
Most of humanity's population, which had been 10 billion strong,

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.810
was lost as a result of worldwide environmental destruction.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.650
The handful who survived could only stand dumbstruck...

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:33.950
...at the foolish end to the war, one that had neither winner nor loser.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:39.740
And then, 15 years passed...

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.480
I guess that's our safe limit.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:11.070
Time to leave!

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:12.070
Roger that!

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:26.040
Jobs where you risk your life sure get the old blood pumping!

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:38.680
All suits have reached minimum safe distance!

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:40.180
Any second now...

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:05.950
<b>After War</b>

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:05.950
<b>GUNDAM</b>

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:13.460
<b>The dream I'd nearly forgotten is beginning to stir,</b>

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:16.420
<b>little by little</b>

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:20.970
<b>filling in the gaps in my heart</b>

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:28.350
<b>The instant my frozen memories begin to awaken,</b>

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:37.860
<b>my only wish is for the future that is about to begin</b>

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.410
<b>I'll reach out with both hands</b>

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:45.410
<b>and embrace that dream I once had</b>

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:49.040
<b>I want to go on believing</b>

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:52.960
<b>without ever letting go or giving up</b>

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:56.590
<b>Until the day comes when I grab hold...</b>

00:02:56.590 --> 00:03:00.470
<b>...of that dream I once had,</b>

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:04.010
<b>I want to keep chasing after it</b>

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:09.910
<b>without ever forgetting my hopes and dreams</b>

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:20.350
<b>Episode 6</b>

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:20.350
<b>"It's Offensive"</b>

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.420
You're better than ever, Ennil El.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:45.090
Electronics and special alloys that can't be manufactured anymore...

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:48.600
With this much treasure, we can live the high life for quite a while.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:52.690
Old U.N.E. power plants are treasure troves.

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:57.230
Everyone stays away because they're afraid of a reactor meltdown,

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:01.110
but ol' Zakot Dattonel hates to see things go to waste.

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:05.990
That's all that power plants that don't supply anyone with power are good for.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.950
Use relics from the war to their fullest...

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:10.830
That's how I do things.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:15.580
And environmental destruction isn't a concern now, not with 10 billion dead.

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:16.920
True

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:22.260
Another job? I had hoped to take some time off.

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:24.760
When you see this, you'll change your mind.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:26.760
You're awfully sure of yourself.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:29.890
This is a... It's a Gundam!

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:31.970
I bought this from an info broker.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:35.900
This is definitely the old U.N.E.'s secret weapon, the GX.

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:38.060
It's nearby, apparently.

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:40.860
This boy is the pilot?

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.030
His name's Garrod Ran.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:46.660
They say he used to hunt mobile suits solo.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:51.120
Anyway, he's an amateur who only started piloting mobile suits recently.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:52.580
I see.

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:57.460
How about it, Ennil? I can't imagine you letting this go.

00:04:57.710 --> 00:05:01.420
You were right. I changed my mind when I saw that photo.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:05.380
What did I tell you? This is a Gundam we're talking about!

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:22.070
Around this same time, the Freeden was heading for a pre-war mobile suit factory...

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:25.280
...based on old U.N.E. data they had obtained.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:30.070
Buying and selling relics of the war.

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:33.790
That was their trade, the Vultures.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:39.080
And their captain, Jamil, had one other objective...

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:43.130
Locating and securing Newtypes.

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:48.510
However, Tiffa Adill was still unable to locate any of them.

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:01.860
There's no need to rush it. Rest a while.

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:03.070
All right.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:07.030
I can't hear anything...

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:14.240
Shouldn't you be working? We're almost at our destination.

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:15.620
Sorry, sir!

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:17.910
Return to your posts.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:20.710
We'll begin working as soon as we arrive.

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:21.920
Is that clear?!

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:22.920
Yes, sir!

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:24.630
Garrod!

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:25.800
Understood!

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:28.010
Everyone return to your posts!

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:29.680
Yes, sir! Yes, sir!

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.060
Sorry, Chief!

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:36.810
We'll finish this up in a jiffy!

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:38.430
Hey!

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:43.810
I don't think I want to let mechanics with zero professional pride...

00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:47.190
...who leave their posts with their jobs undone touch a single screw!

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:50.400
C'mon, don't be so cranky.

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:53.070
Let it slide as a favor to me, the pilot.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.490
That also goes for you, Gundam Boy!

00:06:56.160 --> 00:07:01.580
Everybody knows that real pilots help work on their mechs before a mission!

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:05.170
But I don't really expect that much from you.

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:11.470
We will arrive in 10 minutes. All hands, prepare to start operations.

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:14.850
You heard the lady. Start getting ready.

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:29.440
How's it coming?

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:30.820
We're good over here!

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:42.080
That obnoxious kid makes me so mad...

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:45.500
But I got a chance to see Tiffa, so I guess it was worth it.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:50.720
Seriously, I never see her anymore now that I'm on the crew!

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:52.880
We're ready, Garrod!

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:56.510
It's like Jamil never leaves her side...

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:00.180
And I think there are others who might make a move on her!

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:03.640
Man, what a miscalculation!

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:05.810
Hey, Garrod!

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.150
Yeah?!

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:11.280
Don't just stand there! Start pulling!

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:16.240
Oh, sorry about that! I'll have this wrapped up in no time, so stand aside!

00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:30.590
Take it from here, Garrod!

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:34.720
Sheesh, the people around here are a bunch of slave-drivers!

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:43.100
Oh, no! Garrod, you're pulling too hard!

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:55.740
Guys! Are you okay?!

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:58.410
Oh, man!

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:02.950
Ow!

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:06.420
If you're healthy enough to scream, you're fine.

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:08.670
Who's next?

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:14.510
Um, I...

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:17.840
What's his problem?

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:19.470
Not even an apology?

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:24.310
That probably took all he he had in him.

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:28.480
Oh, right. He's been alone most of his life, right?

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:32.480
I guess living alone in these times will mess with your emotions, too.

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:34.110
No, that's not it.

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:37.150
That's not what I meant.

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:05.930
Garrod...

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:13.940
Fortunately, no one was seriously injured.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:15.280
I see.

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:18.450
Be more careful in the future. Dismissed.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:20.610
His punishment?

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.080
That won't be necessary.

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:25.910
You're a lucky boy, Garrod!

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.040
Don't mess up like that again, okay?

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:30.500
Honestly, you're such a scatterbrain...

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:31.880
Get off my back!

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:36.170
What kind of attitude is that?

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:39.170
Once a stray, always a stray, I guess.

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:44.350
Here is our upcoming schedule.

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:48.480
We set out at first light. Our destination, St. Lange.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:51.650
There, we will sell the mobile suits we collected today.

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:53.440
Understood, sir.

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:55.820
All right, the bridge is yours.

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:02.620
Captain!

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:08.000
If I may ask a personal question?

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:12.580
Um...

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:16.000
My apologies. It's nothing.

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:12.600
Looks like neither one of us is having much luck.

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:49.470
Are you asleep?

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:53.810
Got a minute?

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:59.110
Even you must have heard about what happened with Garrod.

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:05.400
He seems pretty naive deep down, so I bet he's pretty depressed.

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:07.780
Yes...

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:12.080
So it'd be terrible if somebody didn't cheer him up!

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:16.250
And I think that somebody has to be you.

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:20.000
You're pretty without makeup,

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:24.720
but I think if you put some on, got all dolled up, and smiled for him,

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:26.970
it'd cheer Garrod right up!

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:30.430
I... don't know how.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:32.220
Just watch this!

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:37.310
Cheering a boy up is dead simple.

00:13:39.190 --> 00:13:40.400
What'cha think?

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:42.940
Want to try?

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:44.610
No...

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:47.320
Oh. Well, whatever.

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:50.780
I'll leave these here, so try them out if you change your mind.

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:03.250
When you were 15, what did you have on your mind?

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:05.800
I was only thinking of survival.

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:07.380
Oh, right.

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:11.510
For me, that was before the war. We had it easy back then.

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:14.600
As I recall, that was around the time I first fell in love.

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:17.730
She was the only daughter of a civilian military employee.

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:20.690
She was always way out of my league.

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:23.440
Where is she now?

00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:28.400
My memories of her are in here. As for the girl herself...

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:29.950
A colony?

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:31.780
Even higher.

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:33.990
Heaven.

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:35.410
Oh, I see.

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:49.010
When I look at Garrod, I see myself when I was his age.

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:54.560
Always overflowing with emotions, everything seeming so new.

00:14:56.970 --> 00:14:59.140
So, I hear you're not punishing Garrod?

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:04.820
That might be a bad call.

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:06.360
How so?

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:10.950
He doesn't seem to be used to people being nice to him.

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:15.990
If he feels bad about what happened today,

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:20.910
he might do something reckless again.

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:25.210
You think Garrod will do something?

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:29.210
Bingo!

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:35.850
Let's go!

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:40.980
Garrod! Garrod!

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:42.390
Respond!

00:15:43.940 --> 00:15:46.980
Hang on. There are signs that he searched the map database.

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:49.230
Find out where he's going!

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:50.110
Yes, sir.

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:57.700
The GX went out by itself!

00:15:57.740 --> 00:15:58.910
This is our chance! Follow him!

00:15:58.950 --> 00:15:59.910
Yes, ma'am!

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:04.880
Now, then...

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:12.880
I should be able to bring back plenty of goodies from this place!

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:17.720
Garrod is heading there?

00:16:17.800 --> 00:16:21.520
But that's... Isn't that an old U.N.E power plant?

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:26.480
Yes. Not even we Vultures will touch dangerous facilities like that.

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:30.230
If a meltdown starts in the reactor...

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:35.740
He wouldn't!

00:16:36.240 --> 00:16:39.330
You mean he's heading into a power plant without knowing the danger?

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:41.250
Probably so.

00:16:42.700 --> 00:16:45.460
The Freeden will make best speed to minimum safe distance.

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:49.130
Toniya! Notify the surrounding area of the danger by Vulture Sign!

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:50.380
Roger! Roger!

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:01.010
Also, Sara...

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:02.140
Sir?

00:17:02.470 --> 00:17:03.730
Look after things here.

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:06.140
Captain?

00:17:08.810 --> 00:17:11.650
He wouldn't! He's heading out to save that boy?!

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:17.160
Captain!

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:18.570
You're too late.

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:46.480
Oh, dear. Looks like something nasty happened.

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:53.900
I hope a certain moron hasn't started more trouble...

00:17:57.780 --> 00:18:00.200
Okay, let's do this!

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:19.010
Everybody's gonna be so happy!

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:21.510
What?!

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:24.890
I've found you, Gundam!

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:38.240
Who are you people?!

00:18:41.110 --> 00:18:44.450
Watch where you're shooting! If there's a meltdown, we lose everything!

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:08.520
A meltdown's already starting? I screwed up...

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:26.790
Ow! I bit my tongue!

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:29.080
It's better than getting caught in the blast!

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:34.790
Um, we're handing out hazmat suits just in case, but we're shorthanded.

00:19:35.590 --> 00:19:36.710
I'll help out.

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:50.270
Fights where your life is on the line are pretty great, don't you think?

00:19:51.140 --> 00:19:55.110
I'm saying that we both might die before we settle this fight!

00:19:55.190 --> 00:19:56.360
Don't you get it?!

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:03.610
You're finished!

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:07.490
Like hell I am!

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:14.000
This boy is so annoying...

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:19.420
Ennil! Leave this to me!

00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:56.290
She's fast!

00:20:57.630 --> 00:21:00.050
So sorry, but our time is up!

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:03.420
Come back here!

00:21:08.180 --> 00:21:12.390
What the heck? What's happening?

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:20.070
This place... isn't safe!

00:21:20.730 --> 00:21:21.860
What do you mean?!

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:28.030
Thank you, ma'am.

00:21:28.070 --> 00:21:29.120
I'll handle it.

00:21:31.540 --> 00:21:34.370
Tiffa! Just in case, you should put on this hazmat-

00:21:45.510 --> 00:21:48.510
Hurry! Get as far away as possible!

00:21:48.890 --> 00:21:52.600
What the heck is going on?! Is the explosion going to be that bad?

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:54.180
Stop talking, just run!

00:21:54.220 --> 00:21:55.430
All right, fine!

00:22:00.230 --> 00:22:03.570
He's out there risking his life, and here you are...

00:22:10.910 --> 00:22:11.910
It's offensive.

00:22:15.080 --> 00:22:17.040
We're not going to make it...

00:22:17.120 --> 00:22:18.210
What?!

00:22:45.690 --> 00:22:50.990
<b>Can I find the words to tell you</b>

00:22:47.740 --> 00:22:53.180
Garrod's heart aches over an irreparable situation that he himself caused.

00:22:50.990 --> 00:22:56.370
<b>How I live between the walls of steel and stone</b>

00:22:53.740 --> 00:22:57.360
Tiffa, who is also hurt, can offer him no comfort.

00:22:57.360 --> 00:22:59.990
Tormented by grief and loneliness,

00:22:58.040 --> 00:23:04.210
<b>How I close my eyes to find some kind of rapture</b>

00:22:59.990 --> 00:23:02.710
Garrod takes a surprising course of action.

00:23:04.930 --> 00:23:10.570
<b>In a world where you can feel so all alone</b>

00:23:12.240 --> 00:23:17.550
<b>Inside I'm full of light and laughter</b>

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:21.440
<b>There's a flame that burns in me</b>

00:23:21.440 --> 00:23:22.420
<b>(I need a way)</b>

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:26.480
<b>(I need a way) I need a way to set it free</b>

00:23:26.480 --> 00:23:31.400
<b>When you find love in your heart</b>

00:23:31.400 --> 00:23:33.530
<b>(The human touch)</b>

00:23:33.530 --> 00:23:37.590
<b>You can believe from the start</b>

00:23:37.590 --> 00:23:39.580
<b>(From the start)</b>

00:23:40.510 --> 00:23:42.710
<b>Dreams they come true</b>

00:23:42.710 --> 00:23:44.080
<b>(They come true)</b>

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:48.420
<b>All comes to you, oh all at once</b>

00:23:48.420 --> 00:23:52.240
<b>If you believe in human touch</b>

00:23:49.690 --> 00:23:50.920
I'm selling this Gundam!

00:23:50.920 --> 00:23:55.890
<b>Episode 7</b>

00:23:50.920 --> 00:23:55.890
<b>"I'm Selling This Gundam!"</b>

00:23:55.890 --> 00:23:57.890
<b></b>
